      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Alpine Institute, a mission school, educated residents through the 19th and early‑20th centuries, shaping the town’s educational heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpine%2C_Tennessee",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers found the area a hunting ground for Cherokee, especially the Nettle Carrier band, who lived near the creek valleys.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
